    {
      "title": "PSG retains UEFA Super Cup as Doue goal seals 2-1 win over Aston Villa",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/sports/football-news/psg-retains-uefa-super-cup-as-doue-goal-seals-2-1-win-over-aston-villa-126081300354_1.html",
      "description": "Paris Saint-Germain won the UEFA Super Cup for a second straight year by beating Aston Villa 2-1 on Wednesday thanks to Desire Doue's second-half goal in the annual curtain-raiser to the European soccer season.\nDoue's 61st-minute strike after running onto Ousmane Dembele's pass was initially ruled out for offside, only for the goal to be awarded following a video review.\nKhvicha Kvaratskhelia's powerfully struck opener in the 20th was canceled out by a volley from Brian Madjo, a 17-year-old striker making his competitive debut for Villa days after getting approval to play following a dispute with FIFA over his registration.\nIt's the first of a possible six trophies this season for PSG, which became the first team to win back-to-back Super Cup titles since Real Madrid (2016 and '17).\nThe Super Cup is an annual early-season match between the most recent winners of the Champions League (PSG) and Europa League (Villa).\nReferee was the Somali official barred from World CupThe game in .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-13T05:25:08"
    }
